I uploaded NHSound to wuarchive. Its located in /pub/MSDOS_UPLOADS/games
directory and is called nhsound.zip. It will work with ChrHack, a program
which adds graphics to Nethack on PC.

NHSound is a TSR. It takes up little over 50 kb of conventional memory. If
you have enough upper memory, you can load it high by writing lh nhsound at
the command prompt. It also requires 32kb of expanded memory for each sound
(currently it has about 25 sound). 
You can easily add and remove sounds. They are normal .voc files and have a
maximum length of 32kb.
Note that NHSound is still in beta state and has not yet been tested on any
other card than SoundBlaster Pro 2. I'm eager to to hear how it will work
on normal SBs and other compatible boards.

NHSound currently need 50 kb of memory in addition to expanded memory. This
is because it keeps the current sound in conventional memory so that it can
be played through soundboard. If anyone knows how I can output the sound
directly from expanded or extended memory please let me know.

